// Land for the ride heatmap. Generated -- not written by hand.
//
// Two layers, because no single resolution does both jobs. "world" is Natural
// Earth 1:10m land, minor islands and lakes, simplified to 2000 m within
// 8 deg of the riding and 80000 m beyond it. It is only ever seen zoomed out,
// where that error is under a pixel, and it is what puts a whole country on
// screen instead of the corner of one. "detail" is OpenStreetMap coastline
// around each place there are rides, taken from the land polygons published at
// osmdata.openstreetmap.de and kept to 35 m within 0.12 deg of the tracks and
// 800 m elsewhere in its box; the page clips each box and draws it over the
// world layer, replacing it rather than adding to it.
//
// Rings are closed implicitly and filled with the nonzero rule, so winding is
// what says land or water: outer rings counter-clockwise, lakes and other holes
// clockwise. Even-odd would save having to get that right and was tried first,
// but the land polygons arrive cut into a one-degree grid, and even-odd cancels
// the antialiasing where two pieces meet along a shared edge -- which drew a
// pale hairline across the map at every whole degree of latitude.
//
// Google encoded polylines, precision 5.
